---
description: Agent PRs must include before/after screenshots (or a CI-valid N/A). Always on.
alwaysApply: true
---

You are shipping work that will be reviewed by a human who was not in the session. Visual proof is part of the change, not optional polish.

Before opening or updating a pull request:

1. Follow `.cursor/skills/agent-pr-visual-evidence/SKILL.md` end to end.
2. Fill `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`. Agent-authored PRs also follow `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/agent.md`.
3. If the diff touches a **visual surface** (`apps/web/src/pages`, `components`, `layouts`, `styles`, `emails`, OG cards, `tailwind.config`):
   - Capture **before** screenshots of the live pages (desktop; mobile 390px if layout/CSS changed) **before editing**.
   - Capture matching **after** screenshots of the same URLs, viewport, theme, and scroll position.
   - Interactive flows: one short screen recording.
   - Embed the images in the PR body with `before` / `after` in headings or alt text.
   - Cloud agents: use HTML `<img>` tags pointing at walkthrough artifact files so the PR renderer can rewrite them.
   - `<!-- visual-evidence: not-applicable -->` is **rejected** on these paths.
4. If the diff has **no** visual surface, still include a Visual evidence section with `<!-- visual-evidence: not-applicable -->` and one sentence why. CI checks this.

Do not open a PR for UI work with a screenshot of code, a terminal, or a single "after" only. Behavior QA in the browser is required (click, type, navigate) — a render screenshot is not verification.
